import { type } from "arktype";
const Login = type({
email: "string.email",
password: "string >= 8",
...
…
For the digit-must-be-present rule, ArkType uses a narrowing predicate:
```
const Login = type({
email: "string.email",
password: type("string >= 8").narrow(
(s, ctx) => /\d/.test(s) || ctx.mustBe("contain a digit"),
),
"rememberMe?": "boolean",
});
```

